      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taylors_Island%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Ridgeton Farm, another historic landmark on Taylors Island, was listed on the National Register in 1977.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taylors_Island%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 1,120‑acre Taylors Island Wildlife Management Area showcases classic Chesapeake Bay tidal marsh habitat, mixing marsh, forest, and fields.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://dnr.maryland.gov/wildlife/Pages/publiclands/eastern/taylorsisland.aspx",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Wildlife there includes the endangered Delmarva fox squirrel and waterfowl such as Buffleheads, canvasbacks, and scaup.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://dnr.maryland.gov/wildlife/Pages/publiclands/eastern/taylorsisland.aspx",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "A boat ramp on the island provides easy access to the Chesapeake Bay, where locals enjoy crabbing, fishing, and hunting.",
